	(text "The Project Tarkus board is an embedded systems development platform designed for educational and prototyping purposes \nat the Institute of Systems Engineering and Information Technology (UNIFEI).\n\nThe system's core is the STM32G030K6T6 microcontroller (ARM Cortex-M0+), which manages all peripherals and control \nlogic.\n\nThe project integrates several communication interfaces and Human-Machine Interfaces (HMI), making it a versatile tool \nfor learning hardware protocols and firmware programming.\n\nConnectivity: It features a modern USB-C port for power and data, an onboard USB-to-Serial bridge (MCP2200) for easy \ndebugging, a dedicated connector for Bluetooth LE (HM-10) modules, and an SWD interface for programming via ST-Link.\n\nUser Interface (HMI): The board includes an I2C interface for OLED displays, a rotary encoder with a push-button for \nmenu navigation, and two general-purpose LEDs for status indication.\n\nStorage & Timing: It is equipped with an external EEPROM (24LC512) for non-volatile data storage and a 32.768kHz \ncrystal to ensure high precision for the internal Real-Time Clock (RTC).\n\nPower & Expansion: The system is powered via USB with 3.3V regulation and surge protection. Unused pins (including SPI \nand ADC lines) are broken out to an expansion header, allowing for the connection of external sensors and modules."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.018 161.798 0)
		(effects
